            <h2>3. Mastering Debt and Credit Scores</h2>
            <p>Not all debt is bad, but unmanaged consumer debt is a wealth destroyer. In 2026, "Buy Now, Pay Later" (BNPL) services are ubiquitous, making it dangerously easy to fall into a debt trap. Focus on eliminating high-interest liabilities, such as credit card balances, using the Avalanche method (paying highest interest first) or the Snowball method (paying smallest balances first for psychological wins).</p>

            <p>Equally important is monitoring your credit score. A strong credit score dictates your ability to get a mortgage, favorable auto loan rates, and even affects job prospects in certain sectors. Keep your credit utilization below 30% and never miss a payment.</p>

            <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579621970588-a35d0e7ab9b6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80" alt="Smart Spending Behavior" class="article-image">

            <h2>4. Creating Multiple Revenue Streams</h2>
            <p>Depending on a single source of income is the riskiest financial decision you can make today. The world is experiencing rapid transformations in job markets, fueled by AI and automation. Building multiple streams of income—whether it's dividend investing, freelance consulting, creating digital products, or real estate—creates a protective moat around your lifestyle.</p>

